# Omnipod 5 build-time credential — TEMPLATE ONLY (safe to commit; contains no keys).
#
# To embed a credential in your own build:
#   1. Copy this file to  o5credential.txt  in this same folder
#      (that real file is git-ignored and must NEVER be committed — it holds PRIVATE KEYS).
#   2. Replace the placeholder below with your real o5keypair credential (the JSON object with
#      controllerId, intermediateCA, tlsCertificate, privateKey, etc. — see the required fields
#      in O5RegistrationData). To bake in several and have each fresh install pick one at random,
#      put multiple credential blocks separated by a single blank line.
#
# At build time, build.gradle.kts base64-encodes o5credential.txt into
# BuildConfig.O5_EMBEDDED_CREDENTIAL, which the app seeds once on a fresh install
# (SecureO5RegistrationStorage.seedEmbeddedCredentialIfNeeded). If o5credential.txt is absent the
# field is empty and nothing is embedded, so the build behaves exactly as a stock build.
#
# --- replace everything below this line in your real o5credential.txt ---
PASTE_YOUR_O5_CREDENTIAL_JSON_HERE
